  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The Fischer projection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>-erythrose is shown below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/a13475d0-a00a-4ba9-b000-c99cafcad020-image.png\"/> </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>-Erythrose and its isomers are listed as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> in Column I. Choose the correct relationship of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>-erythrose from Column II.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\"><tbody><tr><td> </td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">Column - I</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"> </td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">Column -II</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\">P.</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/bde47f7d-208b-4d26-97e5-35efe0824df6-image.png\"/></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">1.</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">Diastereomer</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\">Q.</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/ce869b1c-50f0-49d4-b011-78b2da04538b-image.png\"/></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">2.</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">Identical</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\">R.</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/6ede1435-51e9-4f87-8700-22fa305fe451-image.png\"/></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">3.</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">Enantiomer</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\">S.</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/3f1300b4-7545-456a-bc1f-0699d05fd392-image.png\"/></td><td> </td><td> </td></tr></tbody></table><p> </p><p> </p>",
